# How this repository releases: the `spa-frontend` archetype's QA slot (`release-request:`, from
# `.config/qits/release-archetypes/spa-frontend.yml` in qits-ci) — install, lint, test (the pact
# specs included), build — plus a `release:` slot of its own, which exists ONLY to publish the
# contracts below.
#
# THE DIRECT PACT (epic qits-965) is this SPA's own consumer contract with qits-projects-service.
# It sits in `pacts/` as `qits-projects-frontend_qits-projects-service.json`, written by the
# `src/app/api/*.pact.spec.ts` specs (regenerate with `QITS_GOLDEN_UPDATE=true npm test`).
#
# THE UI-COMPONENTS PACTS (qits-1284) are the REST calls @qits/ui-components makes on this SPA's
# behalf, declared as contracts keyed by the provider's repository name. They sit flat in `pacts/`
# as `qits-projects-frontend_qits-ui-components-jslib_<provider>.json` (qits-edge-service,
# qits-projects-service, qits-ci-service, qits-githost-service), written by
# `src/app/ui-components.pact.spec.ts` (regenerate with `QITS_GOLDEN_UPDATE=true npm test`). The
# `..._qits-ui-components-jslib_qits-projects-service.json` file is a second pact with the same
# provider, so it rides the existing `qits-projects-service` jar below rather than adding one.
#
# qits-ci packs `pacts/*_<provider>.json` into the maven jar
# eu.wohlben.qits:qits-projects-frontend-pacts-<provider>, which that provider verifies in its own
# gate. A contract package is `if-changed` by definition: a release whose pact with a provider did
# not change publishes nothing for it.
#
# `application:` IS THE APPLICATION THIS SPA BELONGS TO, `qits-projects`. The SPA ships no image and
# is no deployable of its own: qits-projects-service carries it as its Quinoa `webui` submodule and
# serves it from the `qits-projects` application. The pact packages' coordinates are spelled with
# the REPOSITORY names, never this one; `application:` only names the application in the packages'
# description.
#
# WHY THERE IS A `release:` SLOT. The platform publishes contract packages from the release slot's
# last step (the composed postlude), and `spa-frontend` has no release slot — a frontend publishes
# nothing else — so `contracts:` alone composes to UNCOMPOSABLE ("declares contracts but neither it
# nor its archetype declares any 'release' step") and no run at all. Declaring the slot replaces
# only the archetype's (empty) release phase; the QA slot is still the archetype's. The step builds
# nothing: every pact is committed, and the postlude packs and publishes it.
archetype: spa-frontend

contracts:
  application: qits-projects
  pacts:
    qits-projects-service: { packages: [maven] }
    qits-edge-service: { packages: [maven] }
    qits-ci-service: { packages: [maven] }
    qits-githost-service: { packages: [maven] }

release:

  - image: qits/build-images/node-base:latest
    timeout-seconds: 600
    script: |
      # The committed pact is the whole input; the platform postlude below publishes it.
      ls pacts/*_qits-projects-service.json
